### Version info
- Resolved by: #128582
- Merged into: `26.11.1.1486-master` (included in `26.11` and later)
<!-- ch-version-info:end -->

MergeTree on a local disk reads 128 KiB at every isolated granule: end each read at the requested byte ranges (cold ClickBench Q19 -23%, SELECT * point lookup -20%)

### Describe the situation
On a local disk, MergeTree reads a full buffer (up to 128 KiB) at each isolated granule left by index analysis, mostly bytes it never decompresses. The patch gives the local file readers the byte ranges a read can reach, as #122250 does for the reader executor, and ends each read there.

Cold runs (restart, dropped page cache, 120 MiB/s and 3000 IOPS cap, like EBS gp3), 6 paired rounds, median latency, change with 95% CI.

| Query (ClickBench `hits`, 100M rows, 2 parts) | master | patched | change [95% CI] | read from disk | file reads |
|---|---:|---:|---|---:|---:|
| Q19: `WHERE UserID = 435090932899640449` | 506 ms | 390 ms | -22.8% [-24.6%, -20.8%] | 75.5 → 62.9 MiB | 776 → 776 |
| S1: `SELECT *` with the same `UserID` filter | 642 ms | 516 ms | -19.5% [-21.4%, -17.4%] | 86.6 → 71.9 MiB | 1254 → 1252 |
| Q17: `GROUP BY UserID, SearchPhrase LIMIT 10` (control) | 572 ms | 540 ms | -6.4% [-10.4%, -2.2%] | 82.5 → 82.5 MiB | 736 → 729 |
| E1: 5-minute `EventTime` window via a minmax index (control) | 742 ms | 723 ms | -1.1% [-8.4%, +6.8%] | 101.7 → 101.1 MiB | 972 → 974 |
| Q2: full scan of two columns (control) | 155 ms | 150 ms | -3.5% [-7.0%, +0.2%] | 32.0 → 31.9 MiB | 735 → 733 |
| Q36: dashboard on `CounterID = 62` (control) | 156 ms | 152 ms | -2.7% [-3.9%, -1.4%] | 21.9 → 21.8 MiB | 146 → 145 |
| Q40: dashboard on `CounterID = 62` (control) | 111 ms | 112 ms | -2.4% [-10.5%, +6.5%] | 15.0 → 15.2 MiB | 82 → 82 |
| Q41: dashboard on `CounterID = 62` (control) | 101 ms | 102 ms | +0.0% [-3.0%, +3.1%] | 12.4 → 12.4 MiB | 63 → 64 |

With the IOPS cap lowered to 1000 (binaries kept in memory, see the reproduction details), patched/master is Q19 0.92 [0.76, 1.12], S1 1.00 [0.96, 1.05], Q17 0.98 [0.93, 1.05], E1 1.08 [0.96, 1.21] and Q2 0.88 [0.52, 1.47]: no query is significantly slower, and the median number of disk reads is at most 1.4% above master (E1: 850 → 862) and lower for Q19 (677 → 646).

Warm runs (page cache warm, query condition cache off, so every run reads all granules), 6 paired rounds, patched/master:

