<!-- ch-version-info:start -->
### Version info
- Resolved by: #128396
- Merged into: `26.11.1.1047-master` (included in `26.11` and later)
<!-- ch-version-info:end -->

Analyzer: ClickBench Q30 copies aggregate-function documentation and re-resolves the same rewritten sum/count for each of its 90 terms; doing this once makes Q30 9% faster with the columns cache

### Describe the situation
Planning ClickBench Q30 (90 × `SUM(ResolutionWidth + k)`) takes about 24 ms. Each aggregate function lookup copies its registry entry, documentation included, and two analyzer passes resolve and format the same `sum`/`count` replacement for every term. The patch does this work once.

Native warm server, 4-vCPU Graviton3, 100M-row `hits`; each side is the mean of 4 binary copies, 20 rounds × 20 runs; 95% CI.

| Query / workload | Master | Patched | Change [95% CI] |
|---|---:|---:|---|
| Q30, columns cache on (`use_columns_cache = 1`, the default proposed in #123890) | 43.62 ms | 39.67 ms | −9.0% [−10.1%, −8.0%] |
| Q30, current defaults (12 rounds) | 98.73 ms | 95.28 ms | −3.5% [−4.2%, −2.8%] |
| `EXPLAIN PLAN` Q30 (planning only), columns cache on | 24.10 ms | 20.64 ms | −14.3% [−14.8%, −13.9%] |
| Q3 (control), columns cache on | 28.11 ms | 27.99 ms | −0.4% [−2.0%, +1.1%] |
| Q3 / Q8 / Q43 (controls), current defaults | 88.74 / 28.88 / 19.52 ms | 88.84 / 28.75 / 19.65 ms | +0.1% / −0.4% / +0.6%, none significant |
| Q30 peak query memory (`query_log.memory_usage`) | 4.39–4.64 MB | 4.20 MB | lower |

<details><summary>Why it happens and what the patch changes</summary>

With the default codecs, 62% of the server CPU of Q30 is ZSTD decompression of `ResolutionWidth`. With the columns cache that work is gone and planning becomes more than half of the query: `EXPLAIN PLAN` alone takes 24 ms of 44 ms. Three things are repeated for each of the 90 terms:

1. `AggregateFunctionFactory::getImpl` and `tryGetProperties` copy the registry entry (`AggregateFunctionWithProperties`: two `std::function` creators, the `FunctionDocumentation` with its description and examples, the properties) on every lookup. Q30 makes about 270 lookups: 90 during analysis, 178 in the rewrite below, one for `sumCount`. The patch points to the entry instead. This applies to every query that uses aggregate functions.
2. `RewriteSumFunctionWithSumAndCountPass` turns each `sum(x + c)` into `sum(x) + c * count(x)` and resolves `sum`, `count`, `multiply` and `plus` for each term. The patch resolves `sum` and `count` once per column type, and `plus`/`minus`, whose arguments are never constants, once per argument types (the cache is reset when the visitor's context changes). `multiply(c, count(x))` is still resolved for each term because the resolved function depends on the constant.
3. `FuseFunctionsPass` then replaces the 179 equal `sum(x)` and `count(x)` nodes with `tupleElement(sumCount(x), i)`. For each node it formats the AST to keep the original column name as the alias and resolves a new `tupleElement`. Without an alias, all `sum`, `count` or `avg` of one column are equal nodes with equal replacements, so the patch builds the replacement once per function and gives the other nodes copies that reuse the resolved functions and share the `sumCount` node, as before. Nodes with an alias or with a non-column argument keep the existing path.

Hardware counters for 100 × `EXPLAIN PLAN` Q30 in one `clickhouse local` process (startup subtracted): instructions −9.3%, cycles −16.9%. The factory change alone removes 3.5% of the instructions.

Correctness: Q30, `EXPLAIN PLAN` Q30, Q3, Q8 and Q43 return identical results on every binary copy. A 35-statement differential script gives byte-identical output on both builds: `sum`/`count`/`avg` with and without aliases, Nullable, Decimal, Float64 and Int8 columns, constants on either side of `minus`, non-column arguments, GROUP BY/HAVING, joins, scalar and IN subqueries with their own SETTINGS, case-insensitive names, `RESPECT NULLS`/`IGNORE NULLS`, `-State`/`-Merge`/`-If`/`-OrNull` combinators, quantile fusion, window functions, both optimizations disabled, unknown-function errors, and `EXPLAIN QUERY TREE run_passes = 1`. 102 related stateless tests (fusion, `sumCount`, arithmetic in aggregate functions, NULLS actions) have the same per-test result on both builds; the same 9 of them also fail on master in this test environment (missing test clusters, remote shards and test files).

</details>

